Project headers are intentionally kept in one flat include directory so the
firmware can be built without extra include-path management.

Main header groups:

- `pinout.h`: board wiring, GPIO roles, physical robot constants
- `hardware.h`, `timer.h`, `system_timer.h`, `uart.h`, `i2c.h`, `encoder.h`,
  `tb6612fng.h`, `bt_debug.h`: low-level platform and peripheral drivers
- `ir_sensor.h`, `ir_simple_calib.h`, `mpu6050.h`, `sensor_fusion.h`:
  sensing and calibration
- `motion_controller.h`, `pid.h`, `back_align.h`: motion control primitives
- `maze_solver.h`, `flash_storage.h`: navigation and persistence
- `ssd1306.h`, `fonts.h`, `systemTest.h`: user interface and diagnostics

See the repository root `README.md` and `docs/architecture.md` for the
project-level overview.
